### CPU/REGISTER ORGANIZATION ###
CPU/Register Organization means how the registers inside the CPU are arranged and work together to process data quickly.
Simple explanation:
The CPU takes the required data from memory and keeps it in registers.
The ALU does calculations (like addition or subtraction) using the data in the registers.
The answer is kept in a register and can be saved back to memory if needed.
The Control Unit (CU) tells all the parts what to do and when to do it.
